<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Brömsebro (1645)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1645">1645</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Second Treaty of Brömsebro · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torstenson-war">Torstenson War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Brömsebro, signed in August 1645, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torstenson-war">Torstenson War</a> between Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> ceded the Baltic islands of Gotland and Ösel and the Norwegian provinces of Jämtland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harjedalen">Härjedalen</a>, exempted Sweden from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">the Sound</a> tolls and pledged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halland">Halland</a> for thirty years. The treaty marked the shift of power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> from Denmark to Sweden.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bromsebro-1645.jpg" alt="Treaty of Brömsebro (1645)" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kasper Holl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scandinavia_1645.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
